From b88a7cf3259583592ee52edd50737f0413c64812 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 14:00:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): skill chain metadata + generic sub-skill
 registry (W2)

Make Forge skills chain like Superpowers: each skill declares its terminal
state and required successor, and composing skills declare sub-skills through
one generic registry, so the agent flows plan -> dev -> validate -> ship ->
review -> verify, each announcing the next.

Chain metadata is dual-encoded on every skills/<name>/SKILL.md:
- frontmatter keys next/terminal/subskills/handoffs (harness-ignored extras,
  same tolerance already proven by allowed-tools)
- a model-facing HARD-GATE chain line in each stage skill body

Linear ladder: plan->dev->validate->ship->review->verify (verify terminal).
Feeders research->plan and triage-ready->plan. smith orchestrates the six
stages via subskills. Utilities/terminal skills declare terminal:true;
hermes-forge is chainExempt.

Generalize lib/core/runtime-graph.js PLAN_SUBSKILL_DEFINITIONS /
validatePlanSubSkillList into a per-owner SUBSKILL_REGISTRY +
getSubSkillDefinitions/getSubSkillIds/validateSubSkillList; smith resolves
through it. plan's existing sub-skills stay backward compatible.

research owns its Plan-bundle logic; plan references it as a subskill
(inversion). kernel umbrella gains the chain map. .agents/skills mirror
regenerated byte-identical.

New test/skills/chain-integrity.test.js asserts the whole graph.

Issues: skill-chain-metadata-hard-92fecf9f, generic-sub-skill-registry-4529ccc7,
4d4e027c (research/plan inversion)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
